+`.gitmodules` declares repository-level submodules under `references/`. In this working copy the root submodules are checked out (including Builds, Commons, EventStore, FrontComposer, PolymorphicSerializations, Tenants, AI.Tools, and optional Memories). The baseline build/run path depends on the shared build, platform, gateway, UI, serialization, and tenancy source checkouts; `references/Hexalith.Memories` remains optional for rich search. A fresh clone must initialise the baseline root submodules before building/running:
+
+```bash
+git submodule update --init references/Hexalith.Builds references/Hexalith.Commons references/Hexalith.EventStore references/Hexalith.FrontComposer references/Hexalith.PolymorphicSerializations references/Hexalith.Tenants
+# never use --recursive for the default local run
+```
+
+## Entry points
+
+| Purpose | Entry point |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Current local dev / G8 rollback topology | `src/Hexalith.Parties.AppHost/Program.cs` (`dotnet aspire run --project src/Hexalith.Parties.AppHost`) |
+| Target integrated local topology after G8 parity | `references/Hexalith.FrontComposer/src/Hexalith.FrontComposer.AppHost/Program.cs` or an explicitly approved platform AppHost |
+| Domain service host | `src/Hexalith.Parties/Program.cs` → EventStore-only `/process`, `/query`, `/project*`, `/replay-state`, and rebuild routes |
+| MCP host | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Mcp/Program.cs` → `/mcp` |
+| Command handling | `src/Hexalith.Parties/Domain/PartyAggregate.cs` (static `Handle`) |
+| Projection apply | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Projections/Handlers/` (`IDomainProjectionHandler` + folds) |
+| Subscriber reference | `samples/Hexalith.Parties.Sample/PartyEventHandler.cs` |
+
+## Critical-folder cheat sheet
+
+| To change… | Look in… |
+|------------|----------|
+| A command/event/value-object shape | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Contracts/{Commands,Events,ValueObjects,Models}` |
+| Business rules / validation | `src/Hexalith.Parties/Domain/PartyAggregate.cs` + `src/Hexalith.Parties/Validation/` |
+| Read models / search | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Projections/` + `src/Hexalith.Parties/Queries/` |
+| Public client surface | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Client/` |
+| MCP tools | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Mcp/Tools/` |
+| Auth / tenancy / compliance | `src/Hexalith.Parties/{Authentication,Authorization,Compliance,Middleware}` |
+| GDPR encryption/erasure | `src/Hexalith.Parties.Security/` |
+| Current local topology / DAPR rollback wiring | `src/Hexalith.Parties.AppHost/` (retire only after approved platform AppHost parity) |
+| Container publication | `.github/workflows/release.yml`, `scripts/publish-parties-containers.ps1` |
+
+The runner-owned `Hexalith.Parties.Platform.IntegrationTests` project adds a separate
+Platform lane. Run it through `hexalith-module test`; it requires the validated
+environment descriptor and private credential channel and never starts topology.
+
+The `Hexalith.Parties.EventStoreExtensions` project installs owner intent adapters for Development composition. The completed Story 3.3 owner decision makes it packable and not application-publishable; its separate private package-cohort evidence grants no hosted or public-release qualification.
